## Before broker apply

- [ ] Review `tenant-readiness-report.md` and resolve every blocking discovery
  finding, or document an approved exception before using
  `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_ALLOW_NOT_READY=true`.
- [ ] Authenticate Azure CLI to tenant
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:azure.tenantId}}` with permission to manage app registrations,
  service principals, federated credentials, subscription RBAC, and the selected
  backend.
- [ ] Authenticate GitHub CLI to
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.repositorySlug}}` with repository administration,
  Actions variable, environment, and branch-protection access.
- [ ] Confirm the default branch is
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}`.
- [ ] Review the exact plan:
  `pwsh ./bootstrap-broker.ps1` (plan-only by default).
- [ ] Confirm every planned identity is repo-scoped and no OIDC subject contains
  a wildcard.

