## HCW dogfood provenance

- [ ] If this repository is the HCW dogfood instance, store its approved
  configuration in `LZ_DOGFOOD_CONFIG_JSON` and set
  `LZ_DOGFOOD_TENANT_ID`, `LZ_DOGFOOD_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`,
  `LZ_DOGFOOD_PLAN_CLIENT_ID`, and `LZ_DOGFOOD_TERRAFORM_VERSION`.
- [ ] Keep `AZURE_APPLY_CLIENT_ID` and any required `TF_API_TOKEN` scoped to
  protected apply environments.
- [ ] Run render and read-only plan before apply; review the configuration hash,
  every layer log, and destructive-change result.
- [ ] Approve apply only through the exact protected environment and preserve
  `dogfood-report.json` plus independent Azure/state/OIDC/GitHub read-back.
- [ ] Do not mark `dogfoodInstanceAppliesGreen` from code completion, skipped
  execution, render-only output, or plan success.

## Release evidence provenance

- [ ] Preserve the successful, unskipped Factory CI report and successful full
  dogfood apply report for the exact factory version stamped here.
- [ ] Independently review Azure, state, OIDC, active modules, and branch
  protection; bind the approval to both report SHA-256 values using
  `release-attestation.schema.json`.
- [ ] Set `LZ_RELEASE_MAX_EVIDENCE_AGE_HOURS` and
  `LZ_RELEASE_ATTESTATION_JSON`, then run the source factory's manual Release
  Readiness workflow with the exact Factory CI and dogfood run IDs.
- [ ] Treat `LZ_RELEASE_ALLOW_INCOMPLETE=true` as diagnostic only.
- [ ] Change release gates only through a separate reviewed PR after
  `readyForPromotion=true`; the evaluator never promotes automatically.

## Factory CI

- [ ] Confirm the source factory's `Factory CI` check passed for
  the factory version stamped into this repository.
- [ ] Preserve the matching `factory-ci-report.json` as factory release
  provenance.
- [ ] Treat any skipped Terraform/static-analysis check as incomplete evidence,
  not a successful release gate.
- [ ] Confirm the generated repository's own required checks remain enabled;
  Factory CI validates the factory corpus and does not replace customer
  plan/apply protections.

## Apply

- [ ] Set `LZ_CONFIG_PATH` to the exported `lz-config.json`.
- [ ] Set `LZ_DISCOVERY_PATH` to `discovery-inventory.json`.
- [ ] Set `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_OUTPUT` to a protected local output directory.
- [ ] Set `LZ_BOOTSTRAP_APPLY=true`.
- [ ] Run `./bootstrap-broker.sh` or
  `pwsh ./bootstrap-broker.ps1 -Apply`.
- [ ] Preserve `bootstrap-plan.json` and `bootstrap-audit.json` as change
  evidence; neither file contains access tokens.

