## Values never stored in configuration

- Azure user/device login tokens.
- GitHub user/device login tokens.
- `TFE_TOKEN`.
- Any client secret or storage access key.

## Scaffold the generated repository

- [ ] Export `LZ_RENDERED_PATH` with the reviewed renderer output.
- [ ] Export `LZ_SCAFFOLD_TARGET` with a separate local working-tree path.
- [ ] Export `LZ_SCAFFOLD_EVIDENCE` with a protected evidence directory.
- [ ] Run `pwsh ./scaffold-copy.ps1` without `-Apply`; it is plan-only by
  default.
- [ ] Review `scaffold-plan.json` and confirm it targets
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.repositorySlug}}`, branch
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}`, and the approved
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:github.visibility}}` visibility.
- [ ] Confirm the manifest SHA-256 and exact file list match the approved
  renderer output.
- [ ] Authenticate GitHub CLI for repository creation and default-branch push.
- [ ] If the target is non-empty, review it and set
  `LZ_SCAFFOLD_FORCE=true`; the builder preserves a timestamped sibling backup.
- [ ] Set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_CREATE_REPOSITORY=false` if the repository must already
  exist, or `LZ_SCAFFOLD_PUSH=false` for a local-only commit.
- [ ] Optionally set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_REMOTE_URL` and
  `LZ_SCAFFOLD_COMMIT_MESSAGE`, and set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_BRANCH` to override the
  update PR branch.
- [ ] If the repository already exists, use a clean clone of
  `{{FACTORY-RAW:computed.defaultBranch}}` as `LZ_SCAFFOLD_TARGET`; the builder
  pushes an update branch and opens a draft PR instead of pushing the protected
  default branch.
- [ ] Set `LZ_SCAFFOLD_APPLY=true`, then run `./scaffold-copy.sh` or
  `pwsh ./scaffold-copy.ps1 -Apply`.
- [ ] Preserve and review `scaffold-plan.json`, `scaffold-audit.json`, and any
  `*.lz-backup-*` directory.
- [ ] Read back the remote default branch, compare the commit and managed files
  with `scaffold-audit.json`, and approve the first generated-repository PR
  checks before any Terraform apply.

#{{IF deploymentStrategy.mode == 'brownfield'}}
## Brownfield classification and import generation

- [ ] Export `LZ_DISCOVERY_PATH` with a fresh, conclusive, read-only inventory.
- [ ] Export `LZ_BROWNFIELD_CLASSIFICATIONS` with the reviewed classification
  file and `LZ_IMPORT_EVIDENCE` with a protected evidence directory.
- [ ] Run `pwsh ./brownfield-import.ps1` without `-Apply` and review the
  generated classification template, plan, and audit.
- [ ] Review the configured default classification; it is Ignore when omitted.
  Adopt still requires an explicit exact Terraform address and active layer.
- [ ] Classify each candidate as Adopt, Ignore, Replace, or Require-Approval.
- [ ] Provide `approvalReference` for every Replace or Require-Approval entry;
  neither generates mutation.
- [ ] Use `LZ_IMPORT_ALLOW_STALE=true` only under a documented owner exception
  because classifications are pinned to the discovery SHA-256.
- [ ] Set `LZ_IMPORT_APPLY=true` only after approval. Stage 11 writes import
  review artifacts and updates `render-manifest.json`; it never executes
  Terraform import.
- [ ] Review every generated address/ID/layer pair and preserve the discovery,
  classification, plan, audit, and renderer manifest as evidence.
- [ ] Back up state, run a speculative plan, and prove zero unintended destroy
  or replace actions before executing any generated command.
- [ ] Execute generated commands only in an authenticated change-controlled
  operator session. Destructive exceptions require `approved-destroy` plus the
  recorded approval.
#{{ENDIF}}
